    "I now have a clear picture of your setup. Here's what you've got:\n\n**Current architecture on ecb.pm (Hetzner, 4GB RAM, 2 vCPU, 38GB disk):**\n- Caddy reverse proxy (shared, `web` network) — routes `*.ecb.pm` subdomains\n- PostgreSQL 16 (shared, `db` network) — one instance, per-app databases\n- docker-mailserver (own container, already running on `mail.ecb.pm`)\n- Syndiclu app (frontend + backend containers, already live on `syndiclu.ecb.pm`)\n\nThe pattern is clean and well-structured. Each concern is separated.\n\n---\n\n**Re: mail relay — own container or shared?**\n\nYou already have `docker-mailserver` running in its own container, which is the right call. I'd keep it that way. Here's why:\n\n- A mail server has unique resource needs (ports 25/465/587/993, TLS certs, fail2ban, spam filtering) that don't belong in an app container\n- It's shared infrastructure like Caddy and Postgres — all your projects can use `mailserver:587` as their SMTP relay over the `web` or a dedicated `mail` network\n- Isolating it means you can restart/upgrade it without touching any app\n- ClamAV is disabled (good — it would eat your RAM on 4GB), SpamAssassin is on\n\nFor the divingclub app, you'd just configure it to use the mailserver as SMTP relay:\n```\nMAIL_HOST=mailserver\nMAIL_PORT=587\nMAIL_ENCRYPTION=tls\n```\n\nYou'll need to add a mail account or alias for the divingclub to send from. Something like:\n\n```bash\n# On the server, add a sending account\ndocker exec mailserver setup email add noreply@ecb.pm <password>\n```\n\n---\n\n**To add divingclub to this architecture, the plan would be:**\n\n1. Create `/opt/apps/divingclub/` with a `docker-compose.yml` and `Dockerfile` (PHP 8.3-FPM + Laravel app)\n2. Create a database: `docker exec postgres psql -U postgres -c \"CREATE USER divingclub WITH PASSWORD '...'; CREATE DATABASE divingclub OWNER divingclub;\"`\n3. Add a Caddy site file: `/opt/caddy/sites/divingclub.caddy` → `divingclub.ecb.pm { reverse_proxy divingclub-app:8080 }`\n4. Connect the container to both `web` and `db` networks\n\nWant me to start scaffolding the divingclub container setup? I'd create the Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, and Caddy site config.\n[Tool uses: none]",
