    "Here's the situation:\n\n**What you have:**\n- IMAPS (port 993, TLS) — enabled and exposed ✅\n- IMAP (port 143) — listening inside the container but also exposed (should be locked down)\n- POP3/POP3S — not enabled at all. Dovecot protocols are `imap lmtp` only.\n\n**My recommendation: stick with IMAPS, skip POP3.**\n\nPOP3 downloads and deletes mail from the server — not great for an acc environment where you want to check what was sent. IMAPS keeps messages on the server and is the modern standard. It's already running with TLS required and strong ciphers.\n\n**To read mail securely, you have 3 options:**\n\n1. Any mail client (Thunderbird, Apple Mail, Outlook) pointed at:\n   - Server: `mail.ecb.pm`\n   - Port: `993` (IMAPS/SSL)\n   - Username: `admin@ecb.pm`\n   - Password: the one we set earlier\n\n2. A lightweight webmail container (Roundcube) — if you want browser access. Quick to add.\n\n3. CLI check from the server itself:\n```bash\nssh root@ecb.pm \"docker exec mailserver doveadm mailbox list -u admin@ecb.pm\"\nssh root@ecb.pm \"docker exec mailserver doveadm fetch -u admin@ecb.pm 'hdr.subject' all\"\n```\n\n**One thing to tighten up** — port 143 (unencrypted IMAP) is exposed to the internet. Let me close that:\n[Tool uses: execute_bash]",
