    "> great, what can we learn from this process and how should it inform the future newsletter production within the interface ? in parallel, you can resume making sure there is an overview of the scheduled activity in the admin dashboard",
    "\n\nGood question. Let me do both in parallel — the lessons learned report and the scheduled task heartbeat implementation.\n\n## Lessons from the newsletter production process\n\n**What worked well:**\n- The 5-slot compose UI with article picker\n- Decorative SVG elements and scatter button\n- The Blade email template with sliced images\n- Resend as SMTP relay (instant, no hassle)\n\n**What was painful and should be automated in the interface:**\n\n1. **Article link target is hardcoded** — We had to manually swap URLs between `test.clubcep.eu`, `clubcep.eu/joomla/...`, and `clubcep.ecb.pm`. The interface should let you **set a custom URL per slot** (override the auto-generated article link), or at minimum the base URL setting should be more prominent in the compose UI, not buried in Settings.\n\n2. **No bilingual toggle** — We went back and forth on FR-only vs FR+EN. The compose UI should have a **\"Include English translations\" checkbox** that adds the reddish EN cards automatically from the stored translations.\n\n3. **No live email preview** — We sent 6 versions to Gmail before getting it right. The \"Preview Email\" button opens a browser tab, but email rendering is different. Need an **\"Send test to myself\" button** that sends via Resend/SMTP to the logged-in user's email with one click.\n\n4. **Excerpt text not editable** — The card descriptions in the newsletter were auto-generated from article body, but we manually tweaked them (\"Membre du CEP depuis 1984, plus de 1 550 plongées...\"). Each slot should have an **editable teaser text field** that overrides the auto-excerpt.\n\n5. **No per-slot custom link** — For the sorties article, we needed to link to a Joomla registration page, not the article itself. Each slot needs an optional **\"Custom link URL\" field**.\n\n6. **Discount text ended up wrong** — The article content said one thing, the newsletter card said another. The newsletter card text should be **independent from the article body** — it's a teaser, not an auto-excerpt.\n\n7. **Send workflow too manual** — We used `curl` to Resend. The \"Send Newsletter\" button should use Resend's API directly (or whatever relay is configured), not just the local SMTP which was blocked.\n\n**Recommended changes to the compose UI:**\n\n| Feature | Current | Should be |\n|---------|---------|-----------|\n| Card teaser text | Auto-excerpt from article body | Editable text field per slot |\n| Article link | Auto from APP_URL + slug | Editable URL per slot |\n| Language | FR only or manual FR+EN | Checkbox: \"Include EN translations\" |\n| Test send | None (Preview in browser only) | \"Send test to my email\" button |\n| Base URL | Hidden in Settings | Visible in compose header |\n| Send method | Local SMTP only | Resend API / configurable relay |\n\nNow let me implement the heartbeat dashboard while you digest that:\n[Tool uses: execute_bash]",
