    "Here's my assessment — what's worth adding vs what you should skip:\n\n## Worth integrating\n\n| Library | What it does | Why you need it | Effort |\n|---------|-------------|-----------------|--------|\n| **spatie/laravel-permission** | Role & permission management | You have hand-rolled `hasRole()`, `isBureau()`, `CheckRole` middleware. Spatie gives you cacheable permissions, wildcard permissions, Blade directives (`@role`, `@can`), and it's the Laravel standard. Would replace ~50 lines of custom code. | Medium (migration needed) |\n| **spatie/laravel-activitylog** | Audit logging | You have a custom `Auditable` trait. Spatie's version is battle-tested, handles polymorphic relations, has a cleaner API, and supports log cleanup. Could replace your `AuditLog` model + trait. | Medium |\n| **laravel/horizon** | Queue monitoring dashboard | You run queue workers but have no visibility into failed jobs, throughput, or wait times. Horizon gives you a real-time dashboard. Free, by Laravel. | Low |\n| **spatie/laravel-backup** | Backup management | You have a custom `BackupService`. Spatie's handles DB + files, S3 upload, notifications on failure, health checks. More robust than the custom `exec()` + `tar` approach. | Medium |\n| **intervention/image** | Image manipulation | You do face detection and quality scoring with raw GD. Intervention gives you a clean API for resize, crop, watermark, format conversion. Would simplify `ImageQualityService` and avatar handling. | Low |\n\n## Nice to have but not urgent\n\n| Library | What it does | Assessment |\n|---------|-------------|------------|\n| **spatie/laravel-medialibrary** | File/media management | Overkill — your LibraryFile model works fine |\n| **spatie/laravel-translatable** | Model translations | You already have ArticleTranslation with a working system. Switching would be disruptive for little gain |\n| **laravel/sanctum** | API token auth | Only needed if you build a mobile app or external API consumers. Your federation API uses simple key auth which is fine |\n| **spatie/laravel-sitemap** | SEO sitemap | Low priority for a club site |\n| **laravel/scout** | Full-text search | Your `LIKE` queries work fine at your scale (~50 articles, ~100 members). Scout + Meilisearch would be overkill |\n| **spatie/laravel-csp** | Content Security Policy | You already have CSP headers in Caddy. Adding it in Laravel would give per-route control but isn't critical |\n\n## Frontend\n\n| Library | What it does | Assessment |\n|---------|-------------|------------|\n| **TinyMCE or Trix** | Rich text editor | You reference `cdn.tiny.cloud` in CSP but I don't see it integrated. If articles are edited with raw HTML, a proper WYSIWYG would help non-technical bureau members |\n| **SortableJS** | Drag-and-drop lists | Would improve the homepage widget layout editor and newsletter slot ordering. 10KB, no dependencies |\n| **Flatpickr** | Date/time picker | Better than native `<input type=\"date\">` for cross-browser consistency. 15KB |\n\n## Skip entirely\n\n| Library | Why skip |\n|---------|---------|\n| **Livewire/Inertia** | You're Blade + Bootstrap, it works, don't rewrite |\n| **Filament/Nova** | Admin panel frameworks — you already have a complete admin UI |\n| **Telescope** | Dev debugging tool — Debugbar is enough, and Telescope is heavy in production |\n| **Cashier/Stripe** | You use bank transfers + SEPA, not online payments |\n\n## My top 3 recommendation\n\n1. **laravel/horizon** — easiest win, 30 minutes to set up, gives you immediate visibility into your queue workers (medical reminders, backups, email sending). No code changes needed.\n\n2. **intervention/image** — cleans up image handling across avatars, event photos, thumbnails. You're already doing image processing, this just makes it cleaner.\n\n3. **spatie/laravel-permission** — the biggest architectural improvement. Replaces your custom role system with the industry standard. Makes it trivial to add granular permissions later