    "> tell me more about spacie ?",
    "\n\n**Spatie** (spatie.be) is a Belgian web agency from Antwerp that's become the most prolific open-source contributor in the Laravel ecosystem. They maintain 400+ packages, and several are considered the de facto standard for their domain.\n\nThe ones relevant to your project:\n\n**spatie/laravel-permission** (most impactful for you)\n\nWhat you have now:\n```php\n// Hard-coded role checks everywhere\n$user->hasRole('bureau_master')\n$user->isBureau()  // checks 3 slugs\n$user->hasAnyRole(['instructor', 'assistant'])\n// Middleware: role:bureau_master,bureau_finance,bureau_technical\n```\n\nWhat Spatie gives you:\n```php\n// Roles + granular permissions\n$user->hasRole('bureau_master');           // same\n$user->hasPermissionTo('manage equipment'); // NEW — granular\n$user->givePermissionTo('send newsletters');\n\n// Blade directives\n@role('instructor')\n    <button>Mark Availability</button>\n@endrole\n\n@can('manage equipment')\n    <a href=\"/admin/equipment\">Equipment</a>\n@endcan\n\n// Middleware\nRoute::middleware('permission:manage equipment')\n```\n\nThe key difference: right now, if you want someone to manage equipment without being full bureau, you can't. With Spatie, you create a permission `manage equipment` and assign it to any user or role. You can also create custom roles like `equipment_manager` or `newsletter_editor` without touching code.\n\nThe migration would involve:\n- Installing the package + running its migrations (creates `roles`, `permissions`, `model_has_roles`, `model_has_permissions` tables)\n- Migrating your existing `role_id` on users to Spatie's pivot table\n- Replacing `hasRole()`/`isBureau()` calls with Spatie equivalents\n- Updating the `CheckRole` middleware to use Spatie's built-in one\n\nIt's a medium-effort refactor (~2-3 hours) but it's the kind of thing that's easier to do now than later when you have more roles and permissions to manage.\n\n**Other Spatie packages worth knowing about:**\n\n| Package | What it does | Your situation |\n|---------|-------------|----------------|\n| **laravel-activitylog** | Audit logging | You have custom `Auditable` trait — works fine, switching is optional |\n| **laravel-backup** | DB + file backups to S3/local | You have custom `BackupService` — works fine |\n| **laravel-medialibrary** | File/image management with conversions | Overkill for your LibraryFile model |\n| **laravel-translatable** | Model translations | You have ArticleTranslation — different approach but works |\n| **laravel-data** | Typed DTOs | Nice-to-have, not urgent |\n| **laravel-settings** | Typed settings | You have ThemeSetting — similar concept |\n\n**Bottom line:** The only Spatie package I'd strongly recommend is `laravel-permission`. The others would replace working custom code with marginal benefit. The permission system is the one where the standard package is genuinely better than a hand-rolled solution, because permission management gets complex fast once you start adding granular access control.\n\nWant me to do the migration?\n[Tool uses: none]",
