    "\n\nGreat questions. Let me walk through the full flow and then address the domain choice.\n\n## Scenario: Email all participants of the Oman outing\n\n**Step 1 — You're on the event page**\n\nYou're logged in as bureau on `test.clubcep.eu`, viewing the Oman event (let's say event #42). At the bottom, there's a `mailto:` link.\n\n**Step 2 — You click the mail link**\n\nThe link is: `mailto:event-42@clubcep.eu?subject=Oman update`\n\nThis opens your email client (Gmail, Thunderbird, etc.) with:\n- To: `event-42@clubcep.eu`\n- Subject: `Oman update`\n\nYou write your message and hit Send.\n\n**Step 3 — Where does the email go?**\n\nRight now: **nowhere useful**. Here's the problem:\n\n`event-42@clubcep.eu` doesn't exist as a real mailbox. The old CEP system had `members.s42@clubcep.eu` which was handled by a script on the Great-Heberg server. But the new system's `MailAliasService` and `PollInboundMail` only work if the email actually arrives in a mailbox that the app can read.\n\n**The chain that WOULD work with Option A:**\n\n```\nYou send to event-42@clubcep.eu\n    ↓\nclubcep.eu mail server (Great-Heberg) has a catch-all or alias\n    ↓\nForwards to members@ecb.pm (or a dedicated inbound@ecb.pm)\n    ↓\nPollInboundMail job (every minute) reads it via IMAP\n    ↓\nSees To: event-42@clubcep.eu\n    ↓\nMailAliasService::resolve('event-42') → queries EventRegistration for event #42\n    ↓\nGets 8 participant emails from the DB\n    ↓\nSends 8 individual emails via Resend API (from newsletter@clubcep.eu)\n    ↓\nEach participant gets: \"[Event: Oman] Oman update\" with reply-to: your email\n    ↓\nYou get: \"[Sent] Oman update → Event: Oman (8 recipients)\"\n```\n\n## Why `members@ecb.pm` and not `members@test.clubcep.eu`?\n\nYou're right to question this. The answer is: **it doesn't matter which mailbox, as long as the email arrives there.**\n\nThe reason I said `ecb.pm` is because:\n- We already have a working mailserver on `ecb.pm` with IMAP access\n- Creating a mailbox there is one command\n- `test.clubcep.eu` doesn't run a mail server — it's just a web app behind Caddy\n\nBut the actual flow should be:\n\n```\nevent-42@clubcep.eu  →  (forwarded by Great-Heberg)  →  inbound@ecb.pm  →  (IMAP poll)  →  Laravel processes it\n```\n\nThe \"inbound\" mailbox is just a staging area. It could be `inbound@ecb.pm`, `sas@ecb.pm`, or even a Gmail address — the app just needs IMAP access to read it.\n\n**The simpler alternative** that avoids all this forwarding: instead of a `mailto:` link, have a **\"Send to participants\" button** directly in the event page that opens a compose form within the app. The email goes straight through Resend API — no IMAP, no forwarding, no external mailbox needed.\n\nThis is what your existing `EmailController` already does for targeted sends. The `mailto:` approach is the old CEP way (needed because Joomla couldn't send emails). Your new app can.\n\nWant me to add a \"Email participants\" button on the event page that sends directly through the app instead?\n[Tool uses: none]",
