    "> remove the basic auth from staging, but keep the all mail redierected to me. with that redirection, am I still safe if i set the real world email addresses of all the members ?",
    "\n\nYes, you're safe. With `STAGING_MODE=true` and `MAIL_ALWAYS_TO=eddy.collart@gmail.com`, Laravel's `Mail::alwaysTo()` overrides the recipient on every outgoing email at the transport level — the real addresses never reach any mail provider. You can load all real member emails without risk.\n\nLet me remove the basic auth:\n[Tool uses: execute_bash]",
    "There's no basic auth in Caddy — it must be in the Laravel middleware. Let me check:\n[Tool uses: execute_bash]",
