    "\n[Tool uses: execute_bash]",
    "Done. Basic auth is gone — the site is now open. \n\nAnd yes, you're safe to load real member emails because:\n- `STAGING_MODE=true` → `Mail::alwaysTo('eddy.collart@gmail.com')` is set in `AppServiceProvider::boot()`\n- This overrides the `To:` header at the Symfony Mailer level — the real address never leaves the server\n- The original intended recipient still shows in the email body/log, so you can verify who *would* have received it\n[Tool uses: none]",
    "> and symfony is not limited to http but happens before we do the API calls to mailjet or resend right ?",
    "\n\nCorrect. `Mail::alwaysTo()` operates at the Symfony Mailer envelope level — it rewrites the recipient list on the message object *before* it reaches any transport (Resend API, sendmail/Postfix→Mailjet, or anything else).\n\nThe flow is:\n\n```\nMail::to('real-member@example.com')\n  → Symfony Mailer builds the message\n  → alwaysTo() replaces recipient → eddy.collart@gmail.com\n  → Transport sends (Resend API / Postfix→Mailjet)\n```\n\nThe real address never appears in the API call payload or the SMTP `RCPT TO`. It's transport-agnostic — works the same whether the transport is HTTP (Resend), SMTP (Mailjet), sendmail, or log.\n[Tool uses: none]",
